			{
				"id": "post-idempotency-keys",
				"slug": "idempotency-keys",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Idempotency keys, or: how I learned to stop *charging people twice*",
					"date": "2026-07-18T09:00:00.000Z",
					"excerpt": "At-least-once delivery is the only once you get. Here is how to make it safe for money.",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k0",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k1",
									"text": "Every system that moves money eventually charges someone twice. Not because anyone wrote a bug, exactly, but because a phone went into a tunnel at the precise moment the server said “OK”. The client never heard it. So the client asked again.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k2",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k3",
									"text": "This post is about the boring, load-bearing fix: ",
									"marks": []
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k4",
									"text": "Idempotency-Key",
									"marks": [
										"code"
									]
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k5",
									"text": ". The idea fits on a napkin. The edge cases need the rest of the napkin pack.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k6",
							"style": "h2",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k7",
									"text": "At-least-once is the only once you get",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k8",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k9",
									"text": "Networks give you two options: deliver a message zero or more times, or deliver it one or more times. If you want the order to arrive, you pick “one or more”, and then you are responsible for what “more” does to your database.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k10",
							"style": "h2",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k11",
									"text": "The key",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k12",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k13",
									"text": "The client generates a unique key per ",
									"marks": []
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k14",
									"text": "intent",
									"marks": [
										"em"
									]
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k15",
									"text": ", not per request, and sends it with every retry. The server stores the result against that key and replays it instead of doing the work again.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "code",
							"_key": "k16",
							"code": "suspend fun placeOrder(req: PlaceOrder, key: IdempotencyKey): OrderResult =\n    store.getOrPut(key, ttl = 24.hours) {\n        // runs at most once per key. Everything else gets a replay.\n        orders.create(req).also {\n            payments.authorize(it.id, it.total)\n        }\n    }",
							"language": "kotlin",
							"filename": "OrderService.kt"
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k17",
							"style": "h2",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k18",
									"text": "Two requests walk into a bar",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k19",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k20",
									"text": "That ",
									"marks": []
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k21",
									"text": "getOrPut",
									"marks": [
										"code"
									]
								},
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k22",
									"text": " is doing a lot of heavy lifting. If two retries arrive at the same time, both can miss the cache and both can charge the card. You need an atomic claim first, with an explicit in-progress state.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "code",
							"_key": "k23",
							"code": "INSERT INTO idempotency (key, status, request_hash)\nVALUES (:key, 'IN_PROGRESS', :hash)\nON CONFLICT (key) DO NOTHING\nRETURNING key; -- no row back? someone else owns it.",
							"language": "sql",
							"filename": "claim.sql"
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k24",
							"style": "blockquote",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k25",
									"text": "Store a hash of the request body next to the key. Same key with a different body means a client bug, and it deserves a loud 422 rather than a quiet replay of the wrong order.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k26",
							"style": "h2",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k27",
									"text": "TL;DR",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k28",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k29",
									"text": "One key per intent, generated by the client, reused on every retry.",
									"marks": []
								}
							],
							"listItem": "bullet",
							"level": 1
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k30",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k31",
									"text": "Claim atomically, then do the work, then store the result.",
									"marks": []
								}
							],
							"listItem": "bullet",
							"level": 1
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k32",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k33",
									"text": "Fingerprint the request. Reject mismatches.",
									"marks": []
								}
							],
							"listItem": "bullet",
							"level": 1
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k34",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k35",
									"text": "Pick a TTL longer than your longest retry window, then add a day.",
									"marks": []
								}
							],
							"listItem": "bullet",
							"level": 1
						}
					],
					"cover_caption": "fig. 1: a retry, moments before becoming a duplicate charge"
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"tag": [
						"distributed-systems",
						"payments"
					]
				}
			},
			{
				"id": "post-enterprise-tooling-nobody-asked-for",
				"slug": "enterprise-tooling-nobody-asked-for",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Enterprise tooling nobody asked for (and everyone uses)",
					"date": "2026-05-30T09:00:00.000Z",
					"excerpt": "The internal CLI that started as a weekend hack and now has an SLA.",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "k40",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "k41",
									"text": "The internal CLI that started as a weekend hack and now has an SLA.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
